---
/**
 * RefundsContent — Refund Policy body (es/en) for /[lang]/legal/reembolsos.
 *
 * New third legal document (alongside TermsContent/PrivacyContent), same
 * pattern: owner identity from env props, isEs/en branch, fixed "last
 * updated" date from the page. Covers Premium subscription payments only
 * (processed through Paddle, acting as Merchant of Record — see
 * `src/lib/billing/paddle.ts`); course purchases are out of scope today
 * since the "Cursos incluidos" Premium feature is itself not live yet
 * (`UI_LABELS.*.premium.comparison.rows`).
 *
 * The 14-day/renewal-not-used refund terms below are a PROPOSAL the owner
 * must confirm before Premium payments go live — see this change's own
 * report for the full list of points to confirm. Premium payments are not
 * active yet (`PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` unset, `src/lib/env.ts`), so nothing is
 * being charged today; this policy is published ahead of time so it is
 * visible before anyone subscribes.
 *
 * DISCLAIMER: solid industry-standard structure, NOT lawyer-reviewed. Have it
 * reviewed by a legal professional (and confirmed by the owner) before
 * Premium payments go live.
 */
import type { Lang } from '@lib/i18n';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
  ownerName: string;
  ownerRuc: string;
  ownerCity: string;
  ownerEmail: string;
  updated: string;
}

const { lang, ownerName, ownerRuc, ownerCity, ownerEmail, updated } =
  Astro.props;
const isEs = lang === 'es';
---

<div class="legal-prose flex flex-col gap-6 leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
  <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">
    {isEs ? 'Última actualización:' : 'Last updated:'} {updated}
  </p>

  {
    isEs ? (
      <>
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            1. Alcance de esta política
          </h2>
          <p>
            Esta Política de Reembolsos aplica a los pagos de la suscripción
            Premium de ChuyoCode, operado por{' '}
            <strong class="text-zinc-100">{ownerName}</strong>
            {ownerRuc && <>, con RUC N° <strong class="text-zinc-100">{ownerRuc}</strong></>}
            {ownerCity && <>, domiciliado en {ownerCity}, Perú</>}, cuando se
            procesen a través de Paddle. Mientras los pagos de Premium no
            estén activos no se cobra nada, así que todavía no hay ningún pago
            que reembolsar; publicamos esta política de antemano para que la
            conozcas antes de suscribirte.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            2. Tu derecho a reembolso
          </h2>
          <p>
            Puedes pedir el reembolso completo de: (a) tu primer pago de una
            suscripción Premium, dentro de los 14 días siguientes a ese pago;
            o (b) el cobro de una renovación, dentro de los 14 días siguientes
            a esa renovación, si no usaste Premium después de que se cobrara.
            Puedes pedir un reembolso por cada pago, una sola vez.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            3. Cancelación y reembolso son cosas distintas
          </h2>
          <p>
            Cancelar tu suscripción detiene las renovaciones futuras;
            conservas el acceso a Premium hasta el final del período que ya
            pagaste. Cancelar no te devuelve automáticamente el dinero del
            período actual: si quieres eso, debes pedir el reembolso según la
            sección anterior.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            4. Cómo pedir tu reembolso
          </h2>
          <p>
            Puedes pedirlo directamente desde el comprobante o el soporte de
            Paddle (nuestro procesador de pagos y comerciante registrado), o
            escribiendo a{' '}
            {ownerEmail ? (
              <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href={`mailto:${ownerEmail}`}>
                {ownerEmail}
              </a>
            ) : (
              'el correo de contacto del Sitio'
            )}
            , y lo gestionaremos con Paddle. Al ser Paddle quien procesa el
            cobro, también es quien procesa la devolución.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            5. Los términos de Paddle también aplican
          </h2>
          <p>
            Como Paddle actúa como comerciante registrado de esta venta, sus
            propios Términos para compradores (Paddle Buyer Terms) también se
            aplican a tu compra, además de esta política.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            6. Cambios en esta política
          </h2>
          <p>
            Podemos actualizar esta Política de Reembolsos en cualquier
            momento; los cambios rigen desde su publicación en el Sitio.
          </p>
        </section>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            1. Scope of this policy
          </h2>
          <p>
            This Refund Policy applies to payments for ChuyoCode's Premium
            subscription, operated by{' '}
            <strong class="text-zinc-100">{ownerName}</strong>
            {ownerRuc && <>, Tax ID (RUC) No. <strong class="text-zinc-100">{ownerRuc}</strong></>}
            {ownerCity && <>, based in {ownerCity}, Peru</>}, once they are
            processed through Paddle. While Premium payments are not active,
            nothing is charged, so there is nothing to refund yet; we publish
            this policy ahead of time so you know it before you subscribe.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            2. Your right to a refund
          </h2>
          <p>
            You can request a full refund of: (a) your first payment for a
            Premium subscription, within 14 days of that payment; or (b) a
            renewal charge, within 14 days of that renewal, if you did not use
            Premium after it was charged. You can request a refund once per
            payment.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            3. Cancelling is not the same as a refund
          </h2>
          <p>
            Cancelling your subscription stops future renewals; you keep
            Premium access until the end of the period you already paid for.
            Cancelling does not automatically refund the current period's
            payment: if that is what you want, request a refund under the
            previous section.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            4. How to request your refund
          </h2>
          <p>
            You can request it directly from your Paddle receipt or Paddle
            support (our payment processor and Merchant of Record), or by
            writing to{' '}
            {ownerEmail ? (
              <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href={`mailto:${ownerEmail}`}>
                {ownerEmail}
              </a>
            ) : (
              'the Site contact address'
            )}
            , and we will handle it with Paddle. Since Paddle processes the
            charge, it also processes the refund.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            5. Paddle's own terms also apply
          </h2>
          <p>
            Because Paddle acts as the Merchant of Record for this sale, its
            own Paddle Buyer Terms also apply to your purchase, in addition to
            this policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100">
            6. Changes to this policy
          </h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Refund Policy at any time; changes take effect
            upon publication on the Site.
          </p>
        </section>
      </>
    )
  }
</div>
